# A following-error limit above pi never tripped: pid0.pos_error is the
# shortest way from the feedback to the command (-pi..pi), and fault.c
# compared that. A motor that falls behind by more than half a turn read a
# small error again (Yaskawa SGMAH, idm0.max_err 6 rad, 2026-11-17;
# conf/weiler-spindle.txt has max_pos_error 5). fault.c now follows the
# error through the turns (fault0.pos_error_turns). Here the rotor can't
# follow (torque limit below its friction) and the command moves on.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
hv0.sim_f = 0.05
conf0.max_force = 0.01
conf0.max_sat = 0
conf0.max_pos_error = 5
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 3
lcnc 1 150
run 4
fault0.fault
fault0.last_fault
fault0.pos_error_turns
@expect fault0.last_fault == 5
